 "title": "Rolling Detuned Bass",
 "category": "Bass",
 "text": "Sound: a thick, rolling, slightly churning bass of three saws drifting against each other, gliding between notes: the deep bass of big beat and breaks.\n\nHow it's built: three saws an octave down, two of them tuned a little sharp and flat, so they beat and roll; one Slew on the pitch for glides; the Ladder filter low, with a little envelope; a touch of Drive. One voice.\n\nPlay: long notes and slides, legato.\n\nTweak: the TUNE of the two detuned oscillators (more is wider and more churning), the filter's CUTOFF, the Slew's times.",
